    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Ancient History of Haryana includes prominent Indus Valley Civilization sites such as Rakhigarhi and Banawali.",
        "The state was the site of the legendary Three Battles of Panipat that dramatically altered the course of Indian history.",
        "Modern Haryana was created as a separate state on linguistic grounds on November 1, 1966.",
        "Freedom fighters from Haryana played a crucial role in the Revolt of 1857 and the Indian Independence Movement."
